sub:assertion {
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-019> pk:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-019-overall> .
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-019-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Thompson (1917) Ch. VII — tissue cells as hexagons / froth vs. human corneal endothelium (Pass 1 baseline) — MorphoEval overall 54.4/100" ;
        dct:date "2026-10-28"^^xsd:date ;
        dct:description "v1 builds a periodic Voronoi froth morphospace (hexagonal lattice + disorder delta, optional Lloyd relaxation) and computes the froth laws exactly: torus <n> = 6.000, honeycomb mu2 = 0 / excess perimeter 0, P^4 ordering 192 < 256 < 432, Lewis slope, Aboav-Weaire a with the sum rule exact, and a through-centre-cleavage division chain whose fixed point (p6 = 0.434, p5 = 0.267, p7 = 0.221) reproduces Gibson 2006 (0.464 / 0.289 / 0.208) to within 0.03. At the canonical delta = 0.35 the model froth has p6 = 0.343, mu2 = 1.17, excess perimeter 8.95 %. The corneal endothelium specimen and Thompson's Fig. 125 soap froth are shown side by side but NOT segmented, so nothing in v1 measures the claim on tissue. Overall 54.4/100 (faithfulness 44.5, reproducibility 77.5); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit afd867b4c; environment: . Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 62, Morphological realism / specimen match 35, Parameter expressivity 55, Morphometric validation 30, Source and data traceability 85, Code-to-model traceability 72, Reproducibility package 75. Output judged: docs/media/t1917_019_the_forms_of_tissues_or_cell_a_comparison.png: rendered output of thompson/claims/t1917-019_the-forms-of-tissues-or-cell-aggregates.py at afd867b4c, image/png, 834756 B, 1540×990 px, artifact_sha256 592edcce78d6504cb462bf9edd94d2eb6a56495fa38f8fd96aba1429cf8a7c99 (sha256 592edcce78d6504cb462bf9edd94d2eb6a56495fa38f8fd96aba1429cf8a7c99), spec_fingerprint 340ff36032325b8ea801c38e36dff91aa9d34352293527c48827c7e2bd5fb74c. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: 340ff36032325b8ea801c38e36dff91aa9d34352293527c48827c7e2bd5fb74c; artifact_sha256: 592edcce78d6504cb462bf9edd94d2eb6a56495fa38f8fd96aba1429cf8a7c99; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/thompson_1917/t1917-019/elodea_canadensis_leaf_specimen.jpg=ffa66c5d5bfa1afb..., datasets/thompson_1917/t1917-019/human_corneal_endothelium_specimen.jpg=9daed5fb546e11bf..., datasets/thompson_1917/t1917-019/thompson_1917_p322_fig125_126_froth_elodea.jpg=1a31755fe8c43ca4...}. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Thompson p. 305: cellular tissue resembles a froth | Thompson p. 309/323: partitions meet three at a point at ~120 degrees (Lamarle minimal-area condition) | Thompson p. 321: hexagonal pattern illustrated in countless cases but perfectly regular only rarely; eye pigment epithelium as the exemplar | Thompson p. 325: cells on the average hexagonal, some with fewer and some with more sides than six | Thompson p. 330: closely packed hexagons give the minimal extent of boundary in a plane; reconstructed_in_script: Periodic Voronoi froth morphospace with Gaussian positional disorder delta and Lloyd relaxation (not in Thompson) | Euler side-sum, mu2, isoperimetric excess perimeter, Lewis and Aboav-Weaire fits on the model (E1-E5) | Mean-field Gibson 2006 division-topology Markov chain with through-centre cleavage (E6; reconstruction, not Gibson's exact matrix); transfer_boundary: Lloyd (centroidal Voronoi) relaxation is a proxy for surface-tension perimeter minimisation; it is not a Plateau/vertex-model energy descent | The honeycomb bound is applied cell-by-cell to the measured area distribution (Hales 2001 proves the equal-area case); does_not_claim: v1 does not measure any polygon statistic on the corneal endothelium or on Thompson's Fig. 125 | No statement about proliferating epithelia beyond the reconstructed division chain | No scale (um) is attached to the specimen; morphometrics are dimensionless." ;
        dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
        pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
        pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
        pk:evidenceAgainst "open need [independent_assessor/model-fidelity, pressure P=0.5]: Cross-provider second assessor",
            "open need [morphometric_validation/morphometric-validation, pressure P=4.0]: p6, <n>, mu2, CV of area and excess perimeter measured on tissue, with reference norms",
            "open need [parameter_sweep/parameter-expressivity, pressure P=0.5]: delta x Lloyd sweep with p6 / mu2 / excess perimeter curves",
            "open need [specimen_comparison/specimen-match, pressure P=3.0]: Polygon-class overlay of the segmented corneal endothelium next to the model froth at the best-fit delta",
            "remediation needed: {'id': 'R1', 'item': 'Segment the corneal endothelium specimen (blue-channel ridge threshold -> distance-transform watershed), count neighbours of interior cells, measure <n>, mu2, p_n, p6, junction valence, shape index, area CV and excess perimeter on the tissue'}",
            "remediation needed: {'id': 'R2', 'item': 'Render a delta x Lloyd parameter-regime sweep and fit delta to the specimen polygon distribution'}",
            "remediation needed: {'id': 'R3', 'item': 'Add negative/ablation controls: Poisson-Voronoi null, uniform-random cleavage ablation of the division chain, Aboav-Weaire neighbour-shuffle control, rasterised-honeycomb pipeline positive control (pixel perimeter bias calibration)'}",
            "remediation needed: {'id': 'R4', 'item': 'Goodness-of-fit statistics: Pearson r and RMSE between specimen and model/Gibson/honeycomb p_n, chi-square / KS-type distance, bootstrap CI on p6 and <n>, CV of area vs Sheng & Bullimore 2007 norm'}",
            "remediation needed: {'id': 'R5', 'item': \"Digitise Thompson's Fig. 125 A/B through the same pipeline as the physical froth reference\"}",
            "remediation needed: {'id': 'R6', 'item': 'Write datasets/thompson_1917/t1917-019/result.json with the verdict; fix legend/honeycomb-bar overlap; expose --lloyd and --nx on the CLI'}",
            "remediation needed: {'id': 'R7', 'item': 'Independent cross-provider second assessor — still builder-scored'}" ;
        pk:hasScore "0.544"^^xsd:double ;
        pk:hasVerdict "partially faithful" .
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> a pk:Model ;
        rdfs:label "Claude Fable 5.1 (builder-assessor, single-agent Pass 1; cross-provider second assessor pending R7)" ;
        dct:identifier "claude-fable-5-1" ;
        prov:actedOnBehalfOf <https://orcid.org/0009-0007-4948-9192> .
}

